ressure: B handles stress well; C keeps calm in crisis; D maybe not explicit; A maybe not.\n\nDecision-making: A anticipates dangerous situations; C makes correct decisions quickly; D solves problems extremely well.\n\nTeamwork/communication: A very good leadership qualities (leadership is teamwork). Also A sometimes not good at taking criticism, unorganized. B can be uncooperative, grumpy. C difficulty communicating, egocentric, but creates positive atmosphere with crew (that's teamwork). D weak leadership, arrogant, loner.\n\nProfessional development: B excellent computer skills, conscientious; A not open to new ideas; C not willing to further education; D maybe not.\n\nNow weigh.\n\nCandidate A: strong anticipation, complex connections, spatial vision, leadership. Weaknesses: not good at criticism, unorganized. No explicit teamwork strengths beyond leadership; but leadership suggests ability to coordinate. No explicit reliability but maybe implied.\n\nCandidate B: strong stress handling, weather assessment, computer skills, conscientiousness. Weaknesses: grumpy, uncooperative. No explicit teamwork strengths.\n\nCandidate C: 100% reliable, creates positive atmosphere, quick correct decisions, calm in crisis, understands tech. Weaknesses: difficulty communicating, egocentric, not willing to further education. Positive atmosphere suggests teamwork strength despite communication difficulty.\n\nCandidate D: responsibility, concentration, problem solving, responds to unexpected events, but arrogant, weak leadership, loner. No explicit teamwork strengths.\n\nThus candidate C seems to have reliability, positive crew atmosphere, quick decisions, calmness, technical understanding. Communication difficulty is a weakness but positive atmosphere may offset. Candidate A has strong anticipation and leadership but lacks reliability evidence and may be unorganized. Candidate B has stress handling and weather, but teamwork issues. Candidate D has problem solving but attitude issue